{"id":7160,"date":"2024-12-04T15:52:51","date_gmt":"2024-12-04T15:52:51","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/demo.casethemes.net\/industo\/?p=7160"},"modified":"2025-04-21T10:37:51","modified_gmt":"2025-04-21T10:37:51","slug":"borehole-drilling","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/www.kerojetservices.com\/borehole-drilling\/","title":{"rendered":"Borehole drilling by The Pillar&#8217;s Dream-living Foundation in partnership with Kerojet Services Limited"},"content":{"rendered":"\t\t<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"7160\" class=\"elementor elementor-7160\">\n\t\t\t\t        <section class=\"elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-2ead50 elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default ct-header-fixed-none ct-column-none ct-row-scroll-none ct-row-gradient--none ct-row-container--default\" data-id=\"2ead50\" data-element_type=\"section\" data-e-type=\"section\">\n            \n                        <div class=\"elementor-container elementor-column-gap-extended \">\n                    <div class=\"elementor-column elementor-col-100 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-54a84633 ct-column-none col-offset-none\" data-id=\"54a84633\" data-element_type=\"column\" data-e-type=\"column\">\n        <div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n                    \n        \t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c92e1d5 elementor-widget elementor-widget-ct_text_editor\" data-id=\"c92e1d5\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"ct_text_editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"ct_text_editor-c92e1d5\" class=\"ct-text-editor \" data-wow-delay=\"ms\">\n\t<div class=\"ct-inline-css\"  data-css=\"\n        \t\t\">\n\n    <\/div>\n\t<div class=\"ct-text-editor-inner elementor-clearfix\">\n\t\t<p><strong>LOCATIONS:<\/strong><\/p><p>JACOB ADELEYE STREET ODO ERAN ITIRE LAGOS STATE. (JULY 7<sup>TH<\/sup> 2023)<\/p><p>SANGOYOYIN AREA IRAGBIJI, OSUN STATE. (APRIL 7<sup>TH<\/sup> 2024)<\/p><p><strong>INTRODUCTION:<\/strong><\/p><p>The Pillars Dream Living Foundation, a non-profit organization, initiated a project to provide clean water and improve hygiene in JACOB ADELEYE STREET ODO ERAN ITIRE LAGOS STATE and SANGOYOYIN AREA IRAGBIJI. The project focused on drilling a borehole to ensure a consistent and safe water supply, This report provides an overview of the project, its implementation, and the resulting impact on the community.<\/p><p>PROJECT BACKGROUND:<\/p><p>JACOB ADELEYE STREET ODO ERAN ITIRE LAGOS STATE and SANGOYOYIN AREA IRAGBIJI is a community located in the outskirts of Osun state, Nigeria. The community faced challenges in accessing clean water, which negatively affected their health and well-being. The Pillars Dream Living Foundation recognized the need for a sustainable solution and decided to drill a borehole to provide clean and accessible water to the community.<\/p><p><strong>OBJECTIVES:<\/strong><\/p><p>The main objectives of the project were:<\/p><p>a) To provide a consistent and sustainable source of clean water to the JACOB ADELEYE STREET ODO ERAN ITIRE LAGOS STATE and SANGOYOYIN AREA IRAGBIJI.<\/p><p>b) To reduce the prevalence of waterborne diseases and improve overall hygiene in the community.<\/p><p>c) To promote environmental sustainability by reducing the community&#8217;s dependence on surface water sources.<\/p><p><strong>IMPLEMENTATION:<\/strong><\/p><p>a) Site Selection: The Foundation conducted a hydrogeological survey to identify the most suitable location for the borehole. Factors such as water table depth, groundwater quality, and accessibility were considered during the selection process.<\/p><p>b) Drilling and Construction: A professional drilling team was hired to carry out the borehole drilling process. The drilling was completed using a rotary drilling rig, and the borehole was lined with casing to prevent contamination and collapse. A hand pump was installed for easy access to water.<\/p><p>c) Community Engagement: The Foundation engaged community members throughout the project, providing training on water management, hygiene practices, and borehole maintenance. A Water and Sanitation Committee was established to oversee the borehole&#8217;s operation and upkeep.<\/p>\t\t\n\t<\/div>\n<\/div>\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-3505dae5 elementor-widget elementor-widget-ct_text_editor\" data-id=\"3505dae5\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"ct_text_editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"ct_text_editor-3505dae5\" class=\"ct-text-editor \" data-wow-delay=\"ms\">\n\t<div class=\"ct-inline-css\"  data-css=\"\n        \t\t\">\n\n    <\/div>\n\t<div class=\"ct-text-editor-inner elementor-clearfix\">\n\t\t<p><strong>IMPACT:<\/strong><\/p><p>a) Improved Health: With access to clean water, the community experienced a reduction in waterborne diseases such as diarrhea and cholera. Overall health and sanitation in the community improved significantly.<\/p><p>b) Enhanced Quality of Life: The borehole has reduced the time and effort required to collect water, allowing community members, especially women and children, to focus on other productive activities.<\/p><p>c) Environmental Sustainability: The project has contributed to preserving the local environment by reducing the community&#8217;s reliance on surface water sources, which are often prone to contamination.<\/p>\t\t\n\t<\/div>\n<\/div>\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t        <section class=\"elementor-section elementor-inner-section elementor-element elementor-element-1903b3f6 elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default ct-header-fixed-none ct-column-none ct-row-scroll-none ct-row-gradient-